      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The construction of the first schoolhouse sparked the formal establishment of Meyer, turning a cluster of settlers into a village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://iagenweb.org/mitchell/localdat/meyermci.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1900, a new Catholic school rose on Meyer’s current site, reflecting the community’s growing commitment to faith and education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://iagenweb.org/mitchell/localdat/meyermci.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The second floor of that school doubled as the village church for a brief period, serving both spiritual and educational needs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://iagenweb.org/mitchell/localdat/meyermci.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Meyer lies within the Little Cedar River watershed, channeling local streams into Iowa’s broader river system.",
